[{"sha":"49dfd4abbb9f25bd5861d9e1c1bc965905fe8925","node_id":"C_kwDOTM6O99oAKDQ5ZGZkNGFiYmI5ZjI1YmQ1ODYxZDllMWMxYmM5NjU5MDVmZTg5MjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tiago Tavares","email":"tgstavares@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-07T13:47:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"Tiago Tavares","email":"tgstavares@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-07T13:47:20Z"},"message":"Fix proportional IV instruments and multiway covariance precision\n\nRemove exactly proportional instrument columns before fixed-effect absorption\nso CUDA rounding cannot create spurious rank. Preserve near-distinct columns\nand existing identification, estimator and convergence rules.\n\nEvaluate ill-conditioned multiway IV covariance from cluster influences and\nretain wide precision through recovered-intercept scaling and PSD correction.\nSynchronize native source mirrors and metadata for 2.29.3.20261007, and add\npermanent native/Stata regression contracts and validation reports.\n\nValidation: 677 focused native CPU/CUDA contract checks pass. Stata covariance,\nproportional-instrument, repeated-control and first-stage reference contracts\npass; all accepted CUDA cases confirm actual GPU use. Source custody, mirror\nalignment, release metadata, Python/shell syntax and whitespace checks pass.\n\nPerformance: distinct-cluster stress cases cost 8-15% more on local CPU and\nabout 8-13% in concurrent Athena CUDA timings. The report preserves raw timings,\nuncertainty and pending clean-host/full-matrix checks. This is a local\ndevelopment checkpoint; covariance optimization and release qualification\nremain open.","tree":{"sha":"31f1ceec7e0390ef01c7e9503874bd319c648101","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reisportela/xhdfe-xfe/git/trees/31f1ceec7e0390ef01c7e9503874bd319c648101"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reisportela/xhdfe-xfe/git/commits/49dfd4abbb9f25bd5861d9e1c1bc965905fe8925","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://a